From: Phase 1 — Supplier/Customer Balance Fix (cumulative balances)
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(reports): party balances are cumulative through asOfDate, not period movements

Phase 1 scope only. Read-only reporting fix. No schema changes, no migrations.

Root cause: GetPartyBalancesAsync filtered `EntryDate >= from` on a BALANCE, and
NormalizeRange defaults `from` to one month ago. An invoice posted outside that
window with its payment/reversal inside it produced a negative "balance".
GetCashReportAsync in the same file already computes an opening balance correctly;
this brings the party-balance report in line with it.

Direction is now derived from the account's own AccountTypes via the existing
AccountTypesExtensions.Nature(), through a new shared AccountBalanceCalculator,
instead of a caller-supplied isReceivables flag.

Verified behaviour-preserving against DbInitializer seed:
  ReceivablesParent (Id 8,  "1.1.2") => AccountTypes.Assets      => Nature() = Debit  => debit - credit
  SuppliersParent   (Id 10, "2.1")   => AccountTypes.Liabilities => Nature() = Credit => credit - debit
which matches the previous isReceivables:true / isReceivables:false calls exactly.

